  "content_description": "Initiative Action Item",
  "content_text_body": "Stories are a memorable way to communicate that your organization values and celebrates appropriate risk taking. The goal is to create a habit of telling stories that encourage your team to find new and better ways of doing things. This is especially helpful if the stories are examples of frontline employees, or those who don't typically speak up.\n\nWrite out a list of the 5-10 most innovative or beneficial risks that your team or other teams have taken over the past year. Pick the three that best reinforce the importance of taking calculated risks to your collective success. Think about how you would tell them as a story:\n\n* Who was involved?\n\n* When and where did it happen?\n\n* What was happening at the time?\n\n* What was the risk?\n\n* What was the potential consequence of failure?\n\n* Why was it important to take this risk?\n\n* What impact did it have?  \n\nTake a few minutes in meetings and impromptu gatherings to share those stories. See if you can do it once per week for an entire month. Ask team members to share similar stories from their experiences.",
